Z||000000||DJRice||10-02-2001||11:17 PM||||Ive tried tightening the A/C belt.  I have replaced the A/C belt.  The thing will stop squealing for a time and then after a month or so its back at it again.  Tightening that belt is a major PITA...are there any tricks to help out with this one?<P>How tight should I have to get this belt for it to shut up?  This latest noise sounds a bit different then the belt sqealing in the past, is it possible my Compressor Clutch is failing?  If so, is there a way to test it?<P><P>------------------<BR>Dillon<BR>Black '87 SE V6<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/djr_signature.jpg"> <BR>"And this one time, on the Fiero Forum..."||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||10-02-2001||11:57 PM||||The clutch usually works or it doesn't. It's just a couple slabs of metal and an electromagnet.<P>The pulley(s) however may be worn beyond spec. Only fix is replacement.<P>Another real posibility is pulley/belt contamination. replace this belt and clean the pulleys with brake parts cleaner or something like Simple Green or CitriSolv before installing the new one.<P>Also, there is a tool some people have used that they say helps. looks like a big hook with a 1/2 drive hole for a big ratchet or breaker bar. I've seen the tool but I'm not sure just how they use it in that application. (Those of us with serpent belts don't have this problem so I've never had to do one on Fiero...)<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000002||DJRice||10-04-2001||11:18 PM||||Well the update is the AC belt shredded this morning on the way to work so I bet my compressor is frozen.  Oh Joy....||||reg||1
